  "result": "I fixed the bug and the Widget line now gets removed. The demo prints `1` (just the Gadget left), and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:31`, `Cart.remove` compared the SKU you pass in against the item's **name** (`l.item.name != sku`) instead of its **sku**. `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so the filter kept every line. `Cart.add` already matched on `item.sku`, so the two methods disagreed.\n\n**Fix:** a one-word change so `remove` matches on SKU:\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]\n```\n\n**Tests:** `python` and `pytest` aren't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest`. No existing test covers `Cart.remove`, so passing tests don't confirm this fix; the demo output does. I can add a regression test for `remove` if you'd like.",
